+<!--
+  PATCH (spaceplate): WebGPU compat.
+
+  three-viewport-gizmo vendors its own copy of three's fat-line LineMaterial, which
+  extends raw ShaderMaterial. NodeLibrary has no ShaderMaterial mapping, so on
+  WebGPURenderer three logs `Material "LineMaterial" is not compatible` and draws the
+  axis stems as a blank NodeMaterial. Unlike the studio AxesHelper there is no WebGPU
+  build of the vendored material to swap in, so the lines are switched off instead.
+
+  The per-axis `line` option is the library's own supported path. Its option merge
+  (`wt`) only substitutes a default when the user value is `undefined`, so `false`
+  survives; the line builder then destructures `{ enabled, line }` per axis and bails
+  early, leaving the positions array empty and returning null before any LineMaterial
+  is constructed.
+
+  Defaults only set `line: true` on x/y/z (and only for the sphere gizmo), but all six
+  axes are listed so this keeps holding if a future default enables the negatives.
+
+  Only the stems are lost. The handles are MeshBasicMaterial spheres with SpriteMaterial
+  labels -- already WebGPU-safe -- so picking, hover and fly-to all still work.
+-->
+<Gizmo
+  controls={cameraControls}
+  x={{ line: false }}
+  y={{ line: false }}
+  z={{ line: false }}
+  nx={{ line: false }}
+  ny={{ line: false }}
+  nz={{ line: false }}
+/>
